{
 "_syntax_gate": "The mock calls load_table() at startup and logs '!! 读表失败' on bad JSON, then falls back to an EMPTY table -- which looks like 'my edit did nothing'. Always run: python -c \"import json;json.load(open(r'E:\\Test\\Temp\\yqlr\\_out_rrcp\\opcodes_table.json',encoding='utf-8'))\" after editing this file. Beware: a trailing ',,' inside a _schema description string will corrupt the whole file.",
 "_comment": "opcode -> response JSON. 'default' is the fallback for anything unlisted. Edit + restart the mock; no APK rebuild needed. resCode=0 = success; resCode!=0 && !=16001 pops Error_<resCode>. A string in 'data' is shown as a tip popup, so never put a string there on success.",
 "_schema": {
  "10001": "Login. NOTE the nesting: DevelopSystem:syncPlayer(response.data.player) is called with the PLAYER object, so `datas` lives INSIDE data.player, not as a sibling. Getting this wrong makes UnlockSystemListData silently ignored.",
  "datas.HeroesData": "-> HeroModel:synchronize wants {heroes:{<CharacterId>:{...}}}. HeroBase:syncData only needs `next(data)` non-empty to set _owned=true; combat/starId/level/adv/exp/skills/finalProps are all optional. An EMPTY object per hero is enough to own it. IDs must exist in the Character config or DEBUG>0 asserts 'cannot find hero in local dataset'.",
  "datas.Teams": "-> TeamsModel:synchronize wants {maxNum:N, teams:{...}}. _teamsMaxNum starts at 0 and is only raised when maxNum is present, which is why dispatch shows 0/1. NOTE TeamMediator:initMaxHeroNum does `tonumber(GridBattle.BattlePosition) or maxHero`, so the config value wins for a given stage -- GridBattle.BattlePosition=1 for Campaign_C00S01.",
  "datas.UnlockSystemListData": "-> Unlock:synchronize wants {unlockSystemMap:{<systemId>:{...}}}. UnlockSystem:getChatServiceUnlock reads map.Friend_Main and does `data.real`, so Friend_Main must exist or it crashes with 'attempt to index local data'.",
  "datas.TaskCenter": "-> TaskModel:synchronize wants {taskTypeMap:{<TaskCenterType>:{<taskId>:{taskId,taskState,beginCondition,targetValue}}}}. getMainTaskRedPoint runs on the main scene BEFORE the async task requests land, so MainTask must exist up front. Use {} per type: empty means no red dot, and it avoids TaskModelBase:initialize's assert on ConfigReader:requireRecordById('Task', id).",
  "datas.FunctionListData": "optional, cheap, dispatches EVT_TASKCENTER_REDPOINT_REFRESH",
  "datas.StairsBattleData": "-> LadderModel:synchronize wants {typeData:{<type>:{keepingHeroes:{},...}}, checkMaps:{}, todayReward:bool}. LadderSystem:getLadderOnHookHeroes does getLadderInfoForType('COMMON').keepingHeroes with NO nil guard, so ladderList.COMMON must exist or it crashes with 'attempt to index a nil value'. Reached from GuideSystem:checkAutoBattleFuncStatus (line 382) on every battle-failed screen, even with the guide overlay disabled -- the guide code path still executes.",
  "PROBE_note": "Service:newRequest is patched with a cjson.encode nil-detector that dumps params and falls back to '{}'. If you never see [PROBE] lines in logcat, the request encoded fine and the crash was elsewhere.",
  "player.level": "Keep this at 1. PlayerLevelSystem.initialize never calls initData(), so _oldLevel stays nil. checkPlayerLevelUp does `if self._oldLevel < self:getPlayerLevel()` -> 'attempt to compare nil with number'. The level only changes via an upgrade event that calls initData first, which our mock never triggers. Setting level high makes the very first settle crash; level 1 with no exp means the comparison never fires.",
  "19002": "MailService mail list",
  "10036": "story progress",
  "10027": "guide step report (one request per guide step the client walks through)",
  "13015": "seen after entering the tutorial stage",
  "10021": "seen after entering the tutorial stage",
  "41001": "sent right after login",
  "unlock_all": "APK-side: GameConfigs.closeCheckUnlockSystem = true makes Unlock:getIsUnlock always return true. That does NOT cover getChatServiceUnlock, which reads unlockSystemMap directly."
 },
